bug.expected:
- validate_signal_signature never executes, imports or evaluates any part of the source. It parses the source with ast.parse and inspects the syntax tree only.
- The checks it keeps:
  - a module-level def (not async) named the contract's entrypoint;
  - its positional parameters match the contract's (window, seed), with the same names and order;
  - no *args or **kwargs;
  - no default values;
  - the return annotation, when present, is accepted exactly as today.
- It returns the same problem strings as today for each non-conforming case. A SyntaxError still gives "signal source does not compile: ...".
- A module-level statement with a side effect (an import, a call, a loop) is not run. A test proves it: the source writes a sentinel file at module level, and the file never appears.
- _require_signal_module stays available, and is used only by the sandbox's own child load path. No host-side caller of validate_signal_signature, SignalContract.adopt or any signal-agent gate executes the source.
- Every existing contract test and signal-agent adoption test stays green, apart from tests that asserted exec-only behaviour, which are rewritten to the AST equivalent.
